About
This repository contains a pure input/output "bedieneinheit" (HMI panel) built with ESPHome
for Home Assistant. It targets an Olimex ESP32-POE-ISO driving an MPR121 capacitive touch
sensor (12 touch zones: digits 0-9 plus dedicated ARM/DISARM) and an RGB edge-lit backlight
(2 LEDs shining into the laser-cut acrylic edge, lighting up the engraved symbols instead of
individual status LEDs). All alarm logic - PIN validation, arm/disarm state, door contacts,
entry delay, siren, lockout, users - lives in Home Assistant, not on the device.
Meant to be built into a JUNG LS 990 single-gang cover: the face plate stays fully closed,
symbols are only laser-engraved over the touch pads, no through-holes anywhere.
Status: concept / work in progress - see README.md "Open Questions / Roadmap" for what's
still undecided (OLED fit, exact touch zone layout, custom PCB, the HA-side package).

Important Notice
